  "instruction": "Open Visual Studio Code and create a Python script named `cifar10_rgb_variance_ratios.py` under `/home/user/analysis_results/`. In this script: (1) Use the `openml` library to fetch the CIFAR-10 dataset (OpenML ID 40927). (2) Assume each image has three color channels (R, G, B) flattened into 3072-dimensional vectors. (3) Compute the total variance for each channel by summing the per-feature variances. (4) Calculate and save the following ratios in a JSON file named `cifar10_rgb_variance_summary.json`, formatted exactly as `{ \"variance_r_g\": <value>, \"variance_g_b\": <value>, \"variance_r_b\": <value> }`.",
